{#
  Two hops out: what this item is not directly connected to, and the item in
  the middle that connects them.

  Nothing here decides visibility, and nothing here queries. The list is a pure
  derivation from the graph `buildGraph` already filtered at every hop -- a
  private node is never traversed *through*, so an item reachable only by way of
  one is simply absent, with no gap and no placeholder where it was.

  Every hop is printed in the direction it was asserted, with both of its ends
  named, so a hop reads correctly whichever way its edge points and the text
  says exactly what the drawing below draws. All of it is plain text under
  autoescape; nothing here is ever marked safe.
#}
<section class="connected-through">
  <h2>Connected through</h2>
  <p class="hint">
    Not directly connected to this {{ labels.singular | lower }}, but reachable
    by way of something that is. Only what you may see is counted.
  </p>

  <ul class="connection-list">
    {% for connection in connected.items %}
      <li>
        <a href="{{ connection.node.href }}">{{ connection.node.title }}</a>
        <span class="muted small">{{ connection.node.kind }}</span>
        {% if connection.routes.length > 1 %}
          <span class="muted small">· {{ connection.routes.length }} ways through</span>
        {% endif %}

        <ul class="route-list">
          {% for route in connection.routes %}
            <li class="route">
              <span class="route-through">
                through <a href="{{ route.through.href }}">{{ route.through.title }}</a>
              </span>
              {% for hop in route.hops %}
                <span class="hop hop-{{ hop.relation }}">
                  <span class="hop-end">{{ hop.from.title }}</span>
                  <span class="hop-label">{{ hop.label }}</span>
                  <span class="hop-end">{{ hop.to.title }}</span>
                </span>
              {% endfor %}
            </li>
          {% endfor %}
          {% if connection.moreRoutes > 0 %}
            <li class="muted small">
              and {{ connection.moreRoutes }} more way{{ 's' if connection.moreRoutes != 1 }} through
            </li>
          {% endif %}
        </ul>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  {#
    Both notes are about items the viewer may already see. Saying "showing 25
    of 60" withholds nothing -- unlike a marker where a private item was
    filtered out, which is what this application must never print.
  #}
  {% if connected.total > connected.items.length %}
    <p class="muted small">
      Showing the {{ connected.items.length }} most connected of {{ connected.total }}.
    </p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if graphTruncated %}
    <p class="muted small">
      This neighbourhood is larger than the network walks at once, so there may
      be more than are counted here.
    </p>
  {% endif %}
</section>
